If 1208 lacks either R1 endpoint, or 1444 is source-less/only reaches 482 while 751 still reaches 163 and 1221, the rewire failed. Wire UID equality is secondary; endpoint topology is decisive.

My verdict: neither H1 nor H2 survives. The evidence presently favors a partial/broken reroute caused by connecting into already-wired sinks, possibly compounded by Property-node terminal regeneration. I would change my mind only if the endpoint census shows the two exact topologies above.
